🚀 Day 20 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 509 – Fibonacci Number.

This was a simple but important problem for strengthening my understanding of Recursion and how recursive problems can be broken down into smaller subproblems.

💡 Approach: Recursion

The Fibonacci sequence follows:

F(n) = F(n-1) + F(n-2)

I used the base cases:

F(0) = 0
F(1) = 1

For every n > 1, the function recursively calculates the previous two Fibonacci numbers and adds them together.

📚 What I Learned:

✅ Understanding the basic structure of recursive functions
✅ Identifying base cases to stop recursion
✅ Breaking a problem into smaller subproblems
✅ Understanding how recursion naturally represents the Fibonacci relation

⏱️ Time Complexity: O(2^n)
💾 Space Complexity: O(n) due to the recursion call stack

Although this recursive solution isn't the most optimized approach, it helped me understand the fundamental concept of recursion. The next step is to explore Dynamic Programming / Memoization to avoid repeated calculations. 🚀

